---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /insights/
title: "Insights & News | Yentrans Maritime Logistics"
heading: "What the freight desk is learning."
eyebrow: "Insights & News"
seoDescription: "Practical explainers on shipping terms, cargo planning and the developments shaping international trade."
intro: "International logistics changes with trade patterns, vessel capacity, port operations, documentation practices and cargo requirements. Our Insights & News section brings together practical explainers, company perspectives and verified updates that can help shippers make better-informed decisions."
---
<section class="pt-0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid-4 cat-grid">
      <div class="cell-quiet"><h3>Industry Insights</h3><p>Observations about freight planning, global trade and the working realities of shipping.</p></div>
      <div class="cell-quiet"><h3>Trade &amp; Regulatory Updates</h3><p>Verified, dated developments affecting cross-border trade; not legal advice.</p></div>
      <div class="cell-quiet"><h3>The Yentrans Journal</h3><p>Real company milestones, people and operational stories when approved for publication.</p></div>
      <div class="cell-quiet"><h3>Knowledge Hub</h3><p>Practical definitions and guides for importers, exporters and early-career logistics professionals.</p></div>
    </div>

    {% set published = collections.articlesPublished %}
    {% if published.length %}
      <div class="grid grid-3 mt-xl">
        {%- for a in published %}
        <article class="cell reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ a.data.category }}</p>
          <h3><a href="{{ a.url | url }}">{{ a.data.title }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ a.data.excerpt }}</p>
          <p class="meta">{% if a.data.datePublished %}<time datetime="{{ a.data.datePublished | isoDate }}">{{ a.data.datePublished | date }}</time> · {% endif %}{{ a.templateContent | striptags | readingTime }} min read</p>
        </article>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    {% else %}
      {# Six drafts exist and are readable at their own URLs for review, but none is
         listed here: the content pack requires editorial approval before publication. #}
      <div class="notice mt-xl">
        <strong>No articles are published yet.</strong>
        {{ collections.articlesAll.length }} article drafts are written and awaiting editorial
        and factual review. They are not listed or indexed until an approved author is assigned
        and each draft is signed off. Reviewers can read them from the list in
        <code>APPROVALS_NEEDED.md</code>.
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    <p class="disclaimer mt-xl">Shipping requirements and regulatory guidance change. Articles are general
      information and should be checked against the latest rules and shipment-specific professional advice.</p>
  </div>
</section>
